<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ahmed Karamanli</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1686–1745</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ahmed Karamanli was an Ottoman cavalry officer in Tripoli who seized power in 1711, killed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/janissaries">Janissary</a> officers and founded the hereditary Karamanli dynasty of pashas. Recognised by the sultan, he ruled until 1745, extended his authority over <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/fezzan">Fezzan</a> and drew revenue from corsair raiding and trans-Saharan trade. His descendants ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tripoli-greece">Tripoli</a> until 1835.</p></div>
